<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pax Julia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pax Iulia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pax Julia was a Roman town in southern Lusitania, on the site of modern Beja in Portugal's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alentejo">Alentejo</a> region. Founded as a colony in the time of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> or Augustus, it became the seat of one of the province's judicial districts (conventus). Remains of its temple and walls survive, and the town lived on as Beja under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> and the Moors.</p></div>
